    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0677" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Italy/301: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-12-02T13:00:00+01:00">December 2, 1936—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 2—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>503. My 397, October 1, noon.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d488-f1"/> From a variety of
                    well-informed but unofficial sources it is reported that the Italian Government
                    is preparing to inaugurate discussions in Washington looking toward the
                    settlement of its war debts. It is even said that the Minister of Finance has
                    stated that Italy will propose some form of token payment.</p>
                <p>When these reports have been brought to my attention I have refrained from making
                    any comment whatsoever.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
